		'Candidate outcomes: (1) Accepted tsg: sessions.update owns plain mutation/deletion/save/broadcast; compared with a publish-only helper and removed caller coordination. (2) Rejected merging config.update with session updates: config already owns validation, comments, defaults and callback delivery; these are different contracts. (3) Rejected merging cwd/model/autoclose with plain updates: their history, statistics and hard-steering ordering is meaningful. (4) Rejected automatic publication in every tab primitive: tabs.act batches mutation, fork/spawn callers initialize before publication, and sync-session replacement has explicit go-before-close ordering. (5) Rejected replacing intro direct config writes as a pure refactor: config.update would also change comment/default and notification behavior. No speculative behavior changes were included.',
